## Blog Articles

Full articles are in [context/](mdc:context). Read them when you need deeper context for a specific topic.

### BalancerValidatorManager (May 2025)

[Full article](mdc:context/articles/introducing-balancervalidatormanager.md) — Introduces the BalancerValidatorManager smart contract, which extends ACP-99 to support multiple security modules. Enables L1s to progressively decentralize from PoA to PoS at their own pace, without contract migration. Open source, audited by Omniscia.

### Suzaku Airdrop & Season 2 Kickoff (Aug 2025)

[Full article](mdc:context/articles/the-suzaku-airdrop-season-2-kickoff.md) — TGE on Aug 13, 2025. Season 1 airdrop: 4.75M SUZ to 10,000+ users. 50% unlocked + 50% as sSUZ vesting over 6 months. Season 2 started July 31 with SUZ staking (3x multiplier), Blackhole LP, and upcoming L1 launches.

### $1.5M Raise (Aug 2025)

[Full article](mdc:context/articles/suzaku-completes-a-1-5m-raise.md) — Suzaku completed a $1.5M raise across seed round, public sales, and Avalanche Foundation grants. Backed by Blizzard, Yield Yak, Tegridy Capital, 50 Partners, and angels from BENQI, SwissBorg, Chorus One, and Stable Jack.

### L1 LSTs: sALOT (Oct 2025)

[Full article](mdc:context/articles/introducing-suzaku-powered-l1-lsts-with-salot-and-splyr.md) — First deployment of Suzaku core protocol to mainnet. Dexalot is the first L1 integration with a liquid staking token (sALOT). LSTs live on C-Chain, 7-day epochs, rewards in L1 tokens + AVAX + 2.5x Suzaku points.

### Why L1 Decentralization Matters (Dec 2025)

[Full article](mdc:context/articles/why-l1-decentralization-matters-more-than-you-think.md) — Thought leadership by co-founder Gauthier Leonard. Argues that while decentralization seems unnecessary until tested, centralized L1s face catastrophic risk (BLS key compromise → bridged TVL theft). Advocates for Nakamoto coefficient > 2 as minimum, and proposes an L1 stages framework similar to L2BEAT.

